flowchart TB
    accTitle: Proposed webhook delivery architecture
    accDescr: Ingestion accepts only after durable event storage. Processing calls enrichment with bounded concurrency and atomically stores the enriched result and a delivery intent before acknowledging. An outbox relay dispatches delivery work. Delivery retries reuse the enriched payload without reprocessing. Tenant-aware dispatch, bounded retries, and a recovery queue contain failures. Dashboard indexing is asynchronous.
    apps[Customer applications] --> gateway[API gateway: tenant admission limits]
    gateway --> ingestion[Ingestion: validate and durably append]
    ingestion --> bus[(Durable event buffer)]
    bus --> processing[Processing: idempotent work and bounded concurrency]
    processing <-->|Deadline and circuit breaker| enrichment[Enrichment service]
    processing -->|Atomic result and delivery intent, then acknowledge| store[(Event state and delivery outbox)]
    store --> relay[Outbox relay: publish then mark dispatched]
    relay --> queue[(Durable delivery work)]
    queue --> delivery[Delivery: fair tenant dispatch and endpoint limits]
    delivery --> endpoints[Customer webhook endpoints]
    delivery -->|Persist outcome| store
    delivery -.->|Retryable failure: delayed retry with jitter and budget| queue
    delivery -->|Permanent failure or exhausted budget| recovery[(Recovery queue: controlled replay)]
    store --> projection[Asynchronous search projection]
    projection --> index[(Search index)]
    index --> dashboard[Dashboard and API]
    classDef change fill:#e8f3ee,stroke:#387358,color:#172c3a
